@1 = ~Xantam~
@2 = ~Xantam's Minion~
@3 = ~A Letter from Xantam to Eldrith~
@4 = ~My not-so dear Eldrith,

The men have begun preparing the lower passages. They complain about the conditions, the vermin, and the lack of sunlight. I have reminded them that they are thieves, not guests at a noble's manor.

The shipment will be moved through the sewers as you requested. Karne will take care of it. No one in the city suspects what is being transported beneath their feet.

I have also secured several new recruits. They are useful enough, though I remain unconvinced that humanoids possess the necessary discipline to keep their mouths shut. One has already asked whether I intend to share the treasure.

I did not.

The matter concerning the old ruins beneath the city remains unresolved. There are passages there that even my servants refuse to enter. I have no patience for superstition, but something ancient dwells below. If your plans require those chambers, send someone more expendable than myself.

As for the tower you mentioned, I have heard the name Onyx Tower spoken among your agents. I advise caution. Whatever you intend to awaken there, I doubt it will be content to serve you.

Do not mistake my cooperation for obedience, Eldrith.

I have my own interests in this city.

Xantam~

@5 = ~You have failed me for the last time. I have no need for incompetence. Wh—who goes there?~
